{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -la .head-developer && sed -n '1,220p' .head-developer/MEGAPLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"total 120\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 15 meharkhanna  staff   480 May 30 14:08 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 meharkhanna  staff    96 May 30 14:07 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   157 May 30 14:08 ARCHITECTURE.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff  3090 May 30 14:08 CONVERSATION.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   110 May 30 14:08 DECISIONS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   164 May 30 14:08 FLOWCHART.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   538 May 30 14:08 IMPROVEMENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff  5487 May 30 14:07 MEGAPLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   717 May 30 14:08 PROJECT_BRIEF.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   108 May 30 14:08 QUALITY_CHECK.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   117 May 30 14:08 RUNBOOK.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   460 May 30 14:08 TASK_GRAPH.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff    88 May 30 14:08 VALIDATION.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff   131 May 30 14:08 WORKER_HANDOFFS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 meharkhanna  staff  6533 May 30 14:08 state.json\n# Megaplan\n> Generated by the Megaplan skill. Approval is required before the local Codex CLI implementation session starts.\n## Approval Gate\n- Status: Pending user approval\n- To start: reply `approve` in the Codex chat\n- To revise: describe the change before approving\n## Repository\n- Repo: Codexa Smoke Quote Board Two\n- Repo URL: [https://github.com/MeharPro/voice-agent-hackathon.git](https://github.com/MeharPro/voice-agent-hackathon.git)\n- Branch: main\n- Commit: 34c4441\n- Local path: `/Users/meharkhanna/Documents/voice-agent-hackathon/codexa-workspace/generated-projects/codexa-smoke-quote-board-two`\n## User Request\nCreate a new Codexa project named codexa-smoke-quote-board-two and plan a tiny static quote board app with saved favorite quotes.\n## Requirement Summary\nCreate a new Codexa project named codexa-smoke-quote-board-two. Plan a tiny static quote board app with saved favorite quotes. Use a single local Codex CLI session after approval. No secrets, deployment, IAM, backend, auth, or package installation implied.\n## Technical Requirements\n- Architecture/product scope: A compact static quote board with seed quotes, add-quote form, favorite toggles, a favorites filter/view, localStorage-backed persistence, responsive styling, and clear empty states.\n- Assumption: The app is static and browser-only.\n- Assumption: Saved favorite quotes should persist in localStorage.\n- Assumption: No backend, database, auth, checkout, deployment, or external integrations are required.\n- Assumption: Use plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript unless the user revises the plan.\n- Local validation expected: test -f .head-developer/PROJECT_BRIEF.md; test -f .head-developer/TASK_GRAPH.md; test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md; test -f index.html; test -f styles.css; test -f script.js; node --check script.js\n## Proposed Product Direction\nA compact static quote board with seed quotes, add-quote form, favorite toggles, a favorites filter/view, localStorage-backed persistence, responsive styling, and clear empty states.\n## Codex Orchestration\n- One local Codex CLI session owns the repo.\n- Codex decides how many internal subagents are useful; for non-trivial work it should prefer visible named responsibility lanes when that is truthful.\n- Subagents are logical Codex responsibilities, not Docker, VM, GKE, or cloud workers.\n- The user can revise subagent use before approval; approval permits Codex to choose the actual internal count and names.\n- If Codex later determines a materially different subagent strategy is needed, it must stop and ask before changing scope, cost, risk, or timeline.\n- The browser flowchart updates rapidly from a parallel Codex flowchart process and shows only the subagents Codex actually reports.\n## Subagent Check-In\n- Advisor recommendation: use internal Codex subagents when useful.\n- Reason: The Codex planner produced multiple responsibility areas, so internal Codex subagents look useful while keeping one repo and one CLI session.\n- User check-in: Approval means Codex may choose the internal subagent count and names, use multiple named internal subagents when useful, and show those names in the flowchart; tell me before approving if you want a single-lane run.\n- Likely responsibility areas: Project Planning Docs, Static Quote Board UI\n- Advisor source: planner_context\n## Continuous Improvement Loop\n- Codex should look for bugs, UX gaps, performance issues, maintainability problems, missing tests, and feature opportunities while implementing.\n- Codex may implement improvements that fit the approved plan or are required for correctness, validation, safety, or a trustworthy MVP.\n- Codex must record deferred ideas in `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` instead of silently expanding scope.\n- Improvements that materially change scope, architecture, data, cost, risk, or timeline require user approval before implementation.\n## Codex Runtime\n- Model: gpt-5.5\n- Coding reasoning: low\n- Planning/model helper reasoning: gpt-5.5 / low\n- Access: full local access\n- Shell environment: inherited from the local supervisor process\n- Account/config/plugins: same local Codex account and CODEX_HOME configuration used by this machine\n## Proposed Internal Responsibilities\n1. Project Planning Docs - Create/confirm local Codexa planning artifacts and improvement tracking.. Validation: test -f .head-developer/PROJECT_BRIEF.md, test -f .head-developer/TASK_GRAPH.md, test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md.\n2. Static Quote Board UI - Implement the browser-only quote board, favorites behavior, localStorage persistence, and responsive visual polish.. Depends on: Project Planning Docs. Validation: test -f index.html, test -f styles.css, test -f script.js, node --check script.js.\n## Assumptions\n- The app is static and browser-only.\n- Saved favorite quotes should persist in localStorage.\n- No backend, database, auth, checkout, deployment, or external integrations are required.\n- Use plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript unless the user revises the plan.\n## Open Questions\n- None recorded yet.\n## Validation Plan\n- test -f .head-developer/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\n- test -f .head-developer/TASK_GRAPH.md\n- test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md\n- test -f index.html\n- test -f styles.css\n- test -f script.js\n- node --check script.js\n## Completion Bar\n- Files exist in this repo.\n- Validation commands pass or failures are reported honestly.\n- The final summary is grounded in changed files and commands.\n- No docs-only success.\nGenerated: 2026-05-30T21:07:43.029Z\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
